 "Kharos was built to keep time for a city that no longer exists. The city fell and its clocks stopped, but the Hourglass Sentinel still walks its rounds through the empty squares: a bronze giant with a cracked hourglass where its heart should be, the sand inside running upward.\n\nIt fights the way a clock strikes, on the beat and without mercy. Its blade sweeps a half-circle before it like a second hand, and the hero it chooses is held fast while the moment around them stops. Every few seconds it turns the glass, and whatever binds its allies simply runs out.": "Kharosは、もう存在しない都の時を刻むために造られた。都は滅び、時計は止まったが、砂時計の番人はいまも空っぽの広場を巡回している。心臓のあるべき場所にひび割れた砂時計を抱え、その砂は上へと流れる青銅の巨人だ。\n\n時計が時を打つように戦う。拍子どおりに、容赦なく。その刃は秒針のように前方へ半円を描き、選ばれた英雄は周りの一瞬が止まる間その場に縫い留められる。数秒ごとに砂時計を返せば、味方を縛るものはただ尽きて消える。"
